      "artist": "Roger W from Sarasota, Florida, U.S.A.",
      "description": "Queen Emma Bridge in Willemstad is a pontoon bridge across St. Anna Bay (actually an inlet), and now is for pedestrians.  It swings open to let ships enter and leave.  It is now fully open, against the shore on the Otrobanda (west) side.  One of the free ferries that takes people across the bay during bridge openings is partly visible.  I took this photo from a high deck on the cruise ship.  You can see some of the fortifications and another cruise ship, probably Royal Caribbean.  The bridge probably opened for the small tanker in the left background.",
